From ad3a535a2c0cafffaf6a09cdeca550b6e9a28447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:42:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wip: apu-expert-pool P2 -- RAM-budgeted arena on a shared
 pool, a slab that cannot map the machine, and the pool-backed master on an
 integrated device

P2.1: moe_cache_preflight gets a UMA arm.  The arena was refused on a shared pool because
AUTO sizing reads "free VRAM" (on a shared pool: the whole machine), not because the tier is
meaningless -- an expert set larger than RAM has no tier at all without it.  So size it from
MemAvailable instead: MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_MIB (the operator's, and only that) wins, else
MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_UMA_RAM_PCT (60) % of MemAvailable floored at the slab's arena minimum.
MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_UMA=0 restores the pre-campaign refusal verbatim.

P2.2: ggml_cuda_slab_set_total_cap() + the clamp in ggml_cuda_slab_init_locked(): a capped
slab treats the cap as its total *and* as its free figure, so the reserve is sized against the
budget rather than against 121 GiB of GTT.  Without this the slab maps `free VRAM - reserve`
(the 98.44 GiB SLAB_INIT the guard's comment records).

P2.0: ggml_backend_cuda_device_moe_host_master_buft() now offers the pool-backed
(model-mapping) master to an integrated device while -- and only while -- the bounded pinned
pool is armed (new moe_cache_host_pool_enabled() query), because that pool is what serves
every GPU read of it.  With no pool the GPU would read the pageable mapping in place, which
is the fault this campaign started from.

Measured on halo (gfx1151, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, `-ncmoe 8 -lm mmap --host-experts pool`):
masters land in ROCm_HostMap (per-tensor), the arena budget drops 70 695 -> 61 253 MiB, the
run completes with byte-identical greedy text against `-ncmoe 0`, no GPU faults, and the
cache census reports fills=6144 tables=24 arena=3814 MiB.

Two findings that reframe the campaign:
* gate #2 was INERT on this box: moe_cache_shared_pool_device() returns integrated=1 and the
  preflight reaches it, but `--fit` pre-fills g_budget from free VRAM before it, so the arena
  has been running on the APU all along with a ~69 GiB budget.  "The expert cache is refused on
  an APU" was never true here; the real defect is the uncapped budget.  That is what P2.1/P2.2
  address, and it also means this change is the first time the arena on this box is bounded.
* the budget MUST be keyed on the operator's MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_MIB, not on `!g_auto`: the fit
  pass sets g_auto=0 with a free-VRAM figure, so a "no explicit budget" test silently adopts
  the machine (measured 74 489 620 070 B).

Open: the RAM percentage default is unmeasured (60 % of MemAvailable still exceeds free VRAM on
a 123 GiB box -> slab 58.56 GiB); the >RAM acceptance arm has not been run; the UMA INFO line
does not appear in the log although the branch provably runs (cosmetic, census is authoritative).
